+# BRIDGE_REMOTE_INTEGRATION.md
+
+# Remote OpenClaw Bridge integration
+
+This control-center instance includes an adaptation layer for `bot-bridge-service` so that a remote OpenClaw deployment can appear inside the console.
+
+## What this adaptation adds
+
+It introduces a bridge-backed observability source for these panels:
+
+- Overview
+  - Remote Bridge overview
+  - Remote bridge nodes
+- Staff
+  - Remote staff signals
+- Tasks
+  - Remote task evidence
+- Settings
+  - Remote Bridge wiring
+  - Remote Bridge risk summary
+  - Remote bridge nodes
+
+## Data source
+
+The control-center reads a bridge backend through:
+
+- `BRIDGE_CONTROL_BASE_URL`
+- `BRIDGE_CONTROL_TOKEN`
+
+It then proxies that data through internal routes:
+
+- `/api/bridge/overview`
+- `/api/bridge/staff`
+- `/api/bridge/tasks/board`
+- `/api/bridge/tasks/recent`
+- `/api/bridge/errors/recent`
+- `/api/bridge/settings/wiring`
+- `/api/bridge/settings/risk-summary`
+- `/api/bridge/nodes`
+- `/api/bridge/nodes/:nodeId`
+
+## Important boundary
+
+This is an adaptation only.
+
+The control-center source itself comes from:
+- `https://github.com/TianyiDataScience/openclaw-control-center`
+
+The remote bridge support is a local integration layer added so that remote OpenClaw workers and tasks can be shown in the console.
+
+It does **not** replace native usage / memory / docs / subscription sources inside the original control-center design.
+
+## What bridge provides
+
+The bridge-backed panels currently provide:
+- remote worker status
+- remote worker heartbeat health
+- remote task evidence
+- remote dead-letter / error signals
+- bridge wiring state
+- bridge risk summary
+- remote node summaries
+
+## What bridge does not provide directly
+
+The bridge does not directly replace:
+- usage cost / billing sources
+- memory files
+- docs workbench data
+- provider billing snapshots
+- native OpenClaw internal private runtime details
+
+## Deployment note
+
+For stable service startup, use the provided wrapper script:
+- `run-control-center.sh`
+
+And the provided unit:
+- `systemd/openclaw-control-center.service`
